---
description: fleet.yaml inventory, tunnel/loopback-only cloud URLs, Verda+RunPod, idle from client forwards
alwaysApply: true
---

# Fleet invariants

- Inventory: `OLLAMA_ROUTER_FLEET` (`fleet.yaml`) + FleetState + Verda/RunPod.
  YAML tunables only. Top-level YAML `nodes:` → hard config error (wrong file).
- **Cloud providers: Verda and RunPod.** No Thunder, no `THUNDER_*`, no
  `**/thunder/**`, no Thunder admin routes or tests. RunPod is optional
  (`runpod:`, `crates/ollama-router-runpod`, `RUNPOD_API_KEY`).
- Cloud Ollama URLs are **tunnel/loopback-only** (self-hosted zrok **private**
  share). Public `:11434` → `public_url_blocked`, never healthy. Hostname public
  tunnels (`*.zrok.io` etc.) are also rejected. No public-proxy fallback.
  `fleet.yaml` LAN URLs stay direct HTTP (no tunnel on the same L2/L3).
  No Tailscale join. Cloud create does not SSH (Verda startup script / RunPod
  `dockerStartCmd` + enroll).
- Enroll learns the zrok share token via `POST /router/v1/nodes/enroll`
  (fail-closed admin bearer). It must **not** write `fleet.yaml`.
  `origin=verda` / `origin=runpod` only update an existing matching
  `managed_by` FleetState row.
- Idle: `last_client_request_at` only from `inflight_inc` on generate/chat/embed
  and OpenAI `/v1/chat/completions`, `/v1/completions`, `/v1/embeddings`.
  Health, `/api/ps`, capacity, admin, warm-keeper do not count. **Never destroy
  fleet.yaml hosts.** Verda teardown uses `delete_permanently`; RunPod
  terminates pods (never stop-only). Failed destroy retains FleetState
  ownership. Capacity miss → async `create_additional` + **503 + Retry-After**.
- Admin `/router/v1/*`: bearer `OLLAMA_ROUTER_ADMIN_TOKEN`. Unset → 403, no default.

```yaml
# BAD — tunables YAML inventory
nodes:
  - id: local
    url: http://127.0.0.1:11434

# GOOD — tunables only; membership is fleet.yaml + FleetState + cloud managers
policy:
  default_max_inflight: 2
```

See `.opencode/wiki/concepts/ollama-router-product.md`,
`ollama-router-node-tunnel.md`, and `ollama-router-idle-scale-down.md`.
